 "body": "## Summary\n\nThis repository is written mostly by AI agent sessions. This pull request adds the quality bar that keeps that safe: rules that ship with their gates, a knowledge store, an automated reviewer that has to complete before a merge, and server-side merge checks. `guides/quality-bar.md` maps every part to the file, job or setting that implements it, and lists what is not implemented and why.\n\n- **Gates.** One runner, `tools/gates.py`, is the single job in CI and the same command locally. Behind it: the tree gate (what may exist in a public design-phase tree; no credential, no machine-bound string), the knowledge lint, the workflow lint, the assertion that the merge checks are live, and three pull-request gates (title, breadth, answered findings).\n- **Reviewer.** `tools/review/review.py` with `.review/review-rules.yaml`, run by `.github/workflows/review.yml` on `pull_request_target`: the reviewer and its rules come from the base branch, the pull request is data. The required check is the commit status `review`, which only a completed review posts.\n- **Merge.** A ruleset on `main` (`tools/ruleset.json`): pull request required, squash only, every thread resolved, `gates` and `review` green on an up-to-date head, nobody bypasses. `tools/merge_pr.py` merges the exact head that was looked at and carries the gate-flip (`--over-red`) for an item the owner approved.\n- **Proof.** Every decision tool has a `--self-test`; `tools/red_proof.py` replays the recorded mutation behind each proven case on every run (`tools/red_proofs.json`).\n- **Knowledge.** `knowledge/` with `INDEX.md`, four living diagrams, two guides, two skills, and one write-time hook for the one shape that already cost something: writing code in the design phase.\n- **Rules.** `CLAUDE.md` is rewritten so that every rule names its gate, is labelled a HAZARD with an issue (#1 to #7), or is labelled a judgment step. The old rule \"commit the record and push it to `main` after every round\" is retired.\n\n## Blast radius\n\nWhat this change can break, and for whom:\n\n- **Every later change.** `main` no longer accepts a push. A change needs a pull request whose head is green in `gates`, has a `review` status from a completed review, and has every thread resolved. The ruleset is already live; `merge-checks` turns red if it is ever switched off or loosened.\n- **This pull request itself.** The review workflow and its rules are not on `main` yet, so no run can post the `review` status here. It is reviewed off-pipeline, and its merge needs the owner's approval for this item (`merge_pr.py --over-red`).\n- **Agent sessions in this checkout.** The write-time hook denies a write to any path the design phase does not allow. A session that needs a new kind of file has to change `ALLOWED` in `tools/tree_gate.py` first, with a case. The hook fails open on a machine without the `py` launcher (#4).\n- **Pushes from a clone with the hook enabled.** The pre-push hook refuses a commit that holds a credential shape, a drive or profile path, a non-loopback address or an e-mail address, message included. A false positive is fixed in `tools/kit.py` with a case and its red proof, not by skipping the hook.\n- **The owner's Claude seat.** Every non-Draft pull request by the owner, a member or a collaborator starts a review. Without the credential secret that job is red, by design.\n- **Pull requests from outside.** They are not reviewed automatically and stay unmergeable until the owner dispatches the review.\n- **A forge that changes under us.** `merge-checks` is strict: a ruleset parameter that GitHub adds on its own turns the gates red until it is decided and pinned in `tools/ruleset.json`.\n\nWhat it cannot break: there is no product code, and `kurz-design.md` is not touched.\n\n## Checks\n\n- Local, before the push: `tools/gates.py` ran. `tree`, `knowledge`, `ci-config`, `merge-checks` and `push-hook` passed; the three pull-request gates were NOT RUN (no pull request yet); `self-tests` FAILED on the first commit, because the self-tests of `merge_pr.py` and `pr_gates.py` read payloads of a real pull request, which are captured from this one.\n- The pre-push hook ran on the push.\n- The off-pipeline review and the captured payloads follow in this pull request.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
